4)we have a problem that flexbox can fix-> 
if we want to display the content inline then we use inline which displays in the same line or else if we want to display like flex then we use flex which again have many property 
flex-direction to be specified either row or column
then we have align-items(start,center,end) again justify-content(start,center,end,space-around,space-between,space-evenly)
one important thing is divs are displayed on the top of each other where as flex is by default displayed in side by side(stack up on a horizontal axis)
if flex-direction is by default row the justify-content handles the x-axis where as align-items handles the y-axis
where as if flex-direction is column this happens vice versa i.e justify-content handles y-axis and align-items handles x-axis
if align-items are not used in flex-direction row then our items stretches the entire box i.e align-items by default have the value as stretch
justify-content and align items properties only work inside the flex box
